{"name":"Cocobolo","hex":"#784848","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cocobolo","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An oily tropical hardwood of genus Dalbergia from Central America.","An old South American coin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cocobolo"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cocobolo","blocks":[{"text":"Cocobolo is a tropical hardwood of Central American trees belonging to the genus Dalbergia. Only the heartwood of cocobolo is used; it is usually orange or reddish-brown, often with darker irregular traces weaving through the wood. The heartwood changes color after being cut and can be polished to a lustrous, glassy finish. Being quite dense and sometimes having a relative density of over 1.0, it will sink in water. The sapwood is a creamy yellow with a sharp boundary between it and the heartwood."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Cocobolo_chess_pieces.jpg/330px-Cocobolo_chess_pieces.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cocobolo","wikidata":"Q1105430"}],"images":[],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"Ocarina a pistone cocobolo","image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e5/Ocarina_a_pistone_cocobolo.JPG?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","ratio":1.8243243243243243,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ocarina_a_pistone_cocobolo.JPG","share":0.210625},{"title":"Cocobolo Holz","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Cocobolo_Holz.JPG/500px-Cocobolo_Holz.JPG","ratio":1.9627228525121556,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cocobolo_Holz.JPG","share":0.1975},{"title":"Ocarina da tasca cocobolo","image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/4d/Ocarina_da_tasca_cocobolo.JPG?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","ratio":1.2743362831858407,"link":"https://commons.wik